    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13291" root="دهم" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدَّهْمَانُ</span></b>  <i>The night:</i> opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الوَضَّاحُ</span> meaning
“ the day. ” (L in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وضح</span>.) [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثِنْىُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَهْمَانَ</span> <i>The prayer of nightfall:</i> opposed to
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِكْرُ الوَضَّاحِ</span> meaning “the prayer of morning.”
(L and K in that art.: but in the CK and in a
MS. copy of the K, instead of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَهْمَانَ</span> we find
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْمانَ</span>.)

